      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Wait — it’s combat? Declare blockers? But I passed to my turn?\n\nNo — the game went into combat on *their* turn — they’re attacking!\n\nAnd I have only one legal blocker: **Appa, Steadfast Guardian** (3/4 flyer).\n\nIncoming attackers:\n- **Llanowar Elves** — now 4/4? (was 2/2 with a +1/+1/+ — and one more? three in total?)\n- **Gene Pollinator** — 4/5? (was 2/3 with +1/+1)\n- **Ouroboroid** — 4/6? (was 2/4 with +1/+1)\n\nSo three big ones.\n\nI can block one.\n\nBest to block the smallest — the 4/4 Llanowar Elves — Appa (3/4) dies, but I prevent 4 damage.\n\nIf I let it through, I take 4+4+4=12 damage — I die.\n\nBest to block the biggest? Ouroboroid 4/6 — Appa dies, 3 damage prevented — still take 8.\n\nBut maybe I can survive if I block the smallest? No — they all overkill.\n\nWait — total damage: 4+4+4=12 — I’m on 18 — so 6 life after.\n\nBut I have nothing else — no lifegain.\n\nBut no — they’re all 4 power? Llanowar Elves 4/4, Gene Pollinator 4/5, Ouroboroid 4/6 — yes, 4 each.\n\nTotal 12.\n\nI take 12 — go to 6 life.\n\nNot great, but survivable.\n\nIf I block one, I take 8 — go to 10.\n\nBetter.\n\nSo I should block one.\n\nBest to block the one that will die — but all kill Appa.\n\nNo benefit.\n\nBlock the one that helps me most — maybe Ouroboroid is most threatening long-term.\n\nBut all are big.\n\nI’ll block **Llanowar Elves** — maybe it’s the weakest?\n\nNo — all 4 power.\n\nWhatever — I’ll block **Llanowar Elves** with **Appa**.\n\nSo she dies — cute, but gone.\n\nBut I prevent 4 damage.\n\nLet’s do it:\n\n\n\n\n\n",
